Possible pathways include:

- Foundational arithmetic and number patterns.
- Algebra and equations.
- Geometry and spatial reasoning.
- Functions and graphs.
- Probability and statistics.
- Number theory.
- Combinatorics and discrete mathematics.
- Linear algebra.
- Calculus.
- Mathematical logic.
- Proof and mathematical reasoning.
- Further advanced topics when appropriate.

These are potential categories, not a requirement to publish every category immediately.

For every investigation, state prerequisites honestly.

Avoid equating advanced notation with mathematical depth. A well-designed elementary investigation can be just as intellectually valuable as an advanced one.

